---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Sopsdeck — edit secrets locally, ship them encrypted"
  description="Edit SOPS-encrypted dotenv, JSON, and YAML files locally. Grant access with public keys and commit encrypted changes to Git—without a hosted vault."
  active="product"
>
  <section class="hero hero--landing">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <div class="kicker">sopsdeck.com</div>
      <h1>Edit secrets locally. Ship them encrypted.</h1>
      <p>
        Edit SOPS-encrypted dotenv, JSON, and YAML files in a local browser workspace. Grant access
        with public keys, then commit encrypted changes to Git—no hosted vault or shared private
        keys.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="#start">Install with npm</a>
        <a class="button ghost" href="#product">See how it works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <video
      class="hero-video"
      autoplay
      muted
      loop
      playsinline
      poster="/assets/editor.png"
      aria-label="Sopsdeck walkthrough from the product demo catalog"
    >
      <source src="/assets/walkthrough.webm" type="video/webm" />
    </video>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" id="product">
    <article class="card">
      <div class="kicker">Source of truth</div>
      <h2>Your files, on disk</h2>
      <p>
        Projects are folders. Managed Files are dotenv, JSON, and YAML encrypted with SOPS. GitHub
        and CI are destinations, not a second vault.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <div class="kicker">Access</div>
      <h2>Public keys only</h2>
      <p>
        Teammates and CI receive Age public keys. Private keys never go in Git, chat, or a shared
        <code class="mono">.env.keys</code> file.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <div class="kicker">Git</div>
      <h2>Sync, never force</h2>
      <p>
        Commit ciphertext, then Sync: fetch, fast-forward only, push. Diverged branches stop.
        History stays encrypted until you open it.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="split" id="trust">
    <div>
      <div class="kicker">Workspace</div>
      <h2>Folder-first, like a focused editor.</h2>
      <p>
        One sidebar of project folders, files as leaves, values masked until you reveal them.
        Encrypt &amp; save writes only to the local file. The WebView never holds keys on disk.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="product-still">
      <img
        src="/assets/editor.png"
        width="1440"
        height="900"
        alt="Sopsdeck editor with a Production Managed File open"
      />
      <figcaption>Generated still from <code class="mono">./scripts/demo</code>.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="start" id="start">
    <div class="kicker">Install · macOS, Windows, and Linux</div>
    <h2>One npm package. Your browser.</h2>
    <p>
      Install Sopsdeck as a development dependency and run it from any project folder. The package
      downloads the matching native runner on first launch; SOPS is embedded, so there is no Go,
      Rust, Bun, Apple Developer account, or separate SOPS setup.
    </p>
    <pre>npm install -D sopsdeck
npx sopsdeck .

# global shortcut
npm install -g sopsdeck
sd .</pre>
    <p>
      SOPS v3.11.0 is bundled with the local runner. Git remains the only project-level system
      dependency.
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
